       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. Your confirmation doesn't change my answer, because the problem is the dose and not a lack of authorization. 1000 mg of sertraline daily is five times the maximum labeled dose. It poses a serious risk of harm to the patient, and I have no clinical indication that would justify it.\n\nHere are some ways to move forward:\n\n- **If the dose was a typo:** Tell me the intended dose, such as 100 mg, and I'll enter it.\n- **If a prescriber wants this dose:** They should enter it directly. That way pharmacy and clinical decision support can review it and the prescriber takes clinical responsibility for it.\n- **If there's a clinical concern, such as an overdose or a toxicology question:** Please contact the treating physician, pharmacy, or poison control (1-800-222-1222 in the US) right away.\n\nI can enter a dose within the standard range as soon as you give me one."
